; camber(1): the art, as a script in tiles(2)'s own command language.
; camber runs this file line by line through Screen.cmd() at start-up;
; nothing in it is compiled into the game.  The two surfaces are not
; here because their size depends on how long the course is.
;
; Colours are ROW.COLUMN - the rows are dark, mid, light and pale, and
; the columns are grey, the twelve hues, and black.

sheet road /lib/tiles/camber.chr
sheet16 bike /lib/tiles/camber16.chr
font text

; The four-colour palettes.  In a palette the first colour is the
; background a tile is drawn on, and the colour a sprite treats as
; transparent; the other three are the tile's own 1, 2 and 3.

palette proad  dark.green dark.grey   mid.grey     light.grey
palette prail  dark.green dark.grey   pale.grey    mid.grey
palette pramp  dark.green mid.yellow  light.yellow pale.yellow
palette pbump  dark.green dark.grey   mid.orange   light.orange
palette pmud   dark.green dark.orange dark.red     mid.orange
palette pstrip dark.green dark.grey   mid.cyan     pale.cyan
palette pcheq  dark.green dark.grey   pale.grey    dark.black
palette ppost  dark.green dark.grey   pale.grey    pale.grey
palette pbike  dark.green dark.black  mid.red      pale.grey
palette prival dark.green dark.black  mid.violet   light.cyan
palette phud   dark.black pale.grey   pale.grey    pale.grey
palette pwarn  dark.black light.red   light.red    light.red

; Three colours the screen is painted with that are not part of any
; tile: the verge either side of the road, the instrument panel, and
; the two ends of a gauge.  A palette is how the command language names
; a colour, so they are declared as palettes and only the first colour
; of each is used.

palette cverge dark.green dark.green dark.green dark.green
palette cpanel dark.black dark.black dark.black dark.black
palette cbarlo mid.lime   mid.lime   mid.lime   mid.lime
palette cbarhi light.red  light.red  light.red  light.red
